  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137558",
      "title": "Attaching Data To Actions",
      "lectureOrder": 693,
      "videoOrder": 638,
      "sourceHash": "fe1d0f3eab4ed90c23ffee00930c0cbcc75d6cea7d7e81b21d8dbb2610fc85c6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.61,
          "end": 3.63,
          "en": "Now before we'll take",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.63,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "a look under the hood of actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "and see what createAction does under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 11.52,
          "en": "and which alternative code you could write,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.52,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "I also wanna show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 16.14,
          "en": "how you could attach data to your actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.14,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "because it is quite common",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 20.913,
          "en": "that actions should carry some data with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 25.77,
          "en": "For example, in this very simple demo application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.77,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "you might not always want to increase the counter by 1.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 33.363,
          "en": "Maybe you want to add 2 or 3 or 10 to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 36.03,
          "en": "So therefore, you might want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.03,
          "end": 39.87,
          "en": "a more dynamic action that can carry data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 41.22,
          "en": "And since this is so common,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.22,
          "end": 43.77,
          "en": "that, of course, absolutely is a requirement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.77,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "that is supported by NgRx.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "createAction is able to take a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 52.32,
          "en": "which in the end would be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 54.78,
          "en": "that describes the kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.78,
          "end": 57.96,
          "en": "that can be attached to the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.96,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "And that's done with help of the extra props function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 65.31,
          "en": "that's provided by ngrx/store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.31,
          "end": 70.08,
          "en": "Here for this second argument that's passed to createAction,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.08,
          "end": 73.35,
          "en": "you can execute props as a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.35,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "And now the important thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 77.28,
          "en": "is that you add angled brackets here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.28,
          "end": 80.58,
          "en": "since props is a generic function to describe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.58,
          "end": 83.913,
          "en": "the kind of data that can be attached to the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.9,
          "end": 87.12,
          "en": "And this typically is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.12,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "where you could add a key named value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.39,
          "end": 93.27000000000001,
          "en": "though this key name is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.27000000000001,
          "end": 95.58,
          "en": "And you then define the kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.58,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "that can be attached to the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 99.62,
          "en": "For example, here, it would be a number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.83,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "But this can be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "If this would be an action related to user authentication,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "you could instead have an email and a password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 111.87,
          "en": "which both are of type string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.87,
          "end": 114.9,
          "en": "So you really just describe the shape of the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.9,
          "end": 117.33,
          "en": "that should be attachable to the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.33,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "In this case, the value of type number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 124.5,
          "en": "by which the counter should be incremented.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.5,
          "end": 127.14,
          "en": "So that's how you prepare an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.14,
          "end": 130.653,
          "en": "when using createAction for data being attached.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 135.42,
          "en": "To extract this data, you then go to your reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 135.42,
          "end": 137.73,
          "en": "and there in this function that will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.73,
          "end": 141.63,
          "en": "when this action occurs, you can accept a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.63,
          "end": 143.7,
          "en": "an action argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.7,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "And just as the state value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.74,
          "end": 150.74,
          "en": "this action value will be fed in automatically by NgRx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 150.75,
          "end": 154.113,
          "en": "because NgRx is the thing that executes this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 158.4,
          "en": "Now, this action thing, which we're getting here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.4,
          "end": 163.35,
          "en": "turns out to be an object that has a type property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.35,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "and that will simply be the identifier of the action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 170.28,
          "en": "but it then also has a value property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.28,
          "end": 172.32,
          "en": "And it's value here in my case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.32,
          "end": 175.41,
          "en": "because I named this key here value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.41,
          "end": 177.36,
          "en": "when defining the kind of data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.36,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "that can be attached to an action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 181.95,
          "en": "If you chose a different key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.95,
          "end": 183.69,
          "en": "you have to use a different key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.69,
          "end": 185.553,
          "en": "when extracting that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 190.86,
          "en": "So that's how you can extract data from that action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.86,
          "end": 194.283,
          "en": "how you define the data, and how you then extract it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.18,
          "end": 198.39,
          "en": "And with this in the CounterControlsComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.39,
          "end": 200.76,
          "en": "we now would have to pass the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 200.76,
          "end": 203.25,
          "en": "that should be attached to the action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.25,
          "end": 204.87,
          "en": "when calling the action here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.87,
          "end": 207.99,
          "en": "as a function inside of dispatch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.99,
          "end": 210.87,
          "en": "In this case here, it should be an object with a value key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.87,
          "end": 213.75,
          "en": "that could be 2 to increment the counter by 2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.75,
          "end": 216.15,
          "en": "or 5 to increment it by 5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.15,
          "end": 217.56,
          "en": "Whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 217.56,
          "end": 219.213,
          "en": "Here, I'll go with 2.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.32,
          "end": 223.053,
          "en": "And with that, if you run ng serve,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.16,
          "end": 227.57999999999998,
          "en": "you will see that if I reload and I click increment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 227.57999999999998,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "the counter now is incremented",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 232.113,
          "en": "by 2 every time I click this button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 233.34,
          "end": 236.25,
          "en": "And, of course, hopefully unsurprisingly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.25,
          "end": 239.25,
          "en": "this code is exactly the same no matter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.25,
          "end": 242.103,
          "en": "how you are building your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.111,
          "end": 246.13,
          "en": "So I can then also copy over my actions code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 247.74,
          "end": 250.32,
          "en": "into the counter.actions.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 250.32,
          "end": 252.66,
          "en": "and do the same for the reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 252.66,
          "end": 254.67,
          "en": "And the code is exactly the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 254.67,
          "end": 257.1,
          "en": "no matter if you're using standalone components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 257.1,
          "end": 258.693,
          "en": "or Angular modules.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
